      "title": "RDS Engines, Multi-AZ and Read Replicas",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "RDS Engines, Multi-AZ and Read Replicas",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What RDS Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Managed** relational DB, ==no OS or SSH== access",
                "MySQL, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, Oracle, SQL Server, Db2",
                "==Aurora==: MySQL/PostgreSQL-compatible, 6 copies across 3 AZs, grows to 256 TiB"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Multi-AZ vs Read Replica",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Multi-AZ",
                "Read replica"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Replication",
                  "{blue:Synchronous}",
                  "{purple:Asynchronous}"
                ],
                [
                  "Scope",
                  "Same Region",
                  "Can be cross-Region"
                ],
                [
                  "Purpose",
                  "HA / DR",
                  "Read scaling"
                ],
                [
                  "Reads",
                  "None from standby",
                  "Own endpoint"
                ],
                [
                  "Failover",
                  "==Automatic==",
                  "None, promote it"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 4
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Primary fails",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "DNS flips",
                    "sub": "same endpoint",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Standby serves",
                    "sub": "~1-2 min",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Multi-AZ DB cluster (two readable standbys) is the ==exception==: standbys serve reads",
                "Replicas: up to ==15== (MySQL/PostgreSQL/MariaDB, Aurora), ==5== (Oracle, SQL Server)",
                "Replica can be ==promoted== to a standalone DB; ==lag== is possible"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Counting a replica as your failover",
                "Sending writes to a replica",
                "Expecting strictly fresh async reads"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Multi-AZ for scaling?** No, HA only; standby serves no reads",
                "**Cross-Region read DR?** Cross-Region read replica",
                "**Stale replica read?** Async replication lag",
                "**Endpoint on failover?** Same DNS name flips to standby"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "RDS Backups and Recovery",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "RDS Backups and Recovery",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Automated vs Manual",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Automated",
                "Manual snapshot"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Made by",
                  "Daily snapshot + logs",
                  "You"
                ],
                [
                  "Retention",
                  "==1-35== days (default **7**)",
                  "Until you delete"
                ],
                [
                  "DB deleted",
                  "Removed unless retained",
                  "{green:Survives}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==PITR== restores to any second in the window",
                "Retention `0` turns automated backups **off**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Restore and Copy",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Snapshot or PITR",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New instance",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New endpoint",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Repoint app",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Snapshots copy across ==Regions==",
                "Snapshots share across ==accounts==",
                "Encryption **cannot** be removed from a DB"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Encrypt an unencrypted DB",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Snapshot",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Copy with KMS key",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Restore the copy",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Expecting an ==in-place== restore",
                "Relying on automated backups after **deleting** the DB",
                "Disabling backups on a source with ==read replicas=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Restore never overwrites",
              "text": "Every restore makes a ==new instance== with a new endpoint. Repoint the app, then retire the old DB."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
