    {
      "title": "DynamoDB Tables, Keys and GSIs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "DynamoDB Tables, Keys and GSIs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Keys",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Serverless== key-value/document NoSQL, single-digit-ms latency",
                "Item limit ==400 KB==",
                "Primary key: **partition key**, or partition + **sort key**",
                "Partition key is ==hashed== to pick the partition"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Good}: high-cardinality, evenly accessed key",
                "{red:Bad}: `status` or date → hot partition, throttling"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Query vs Scan",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sort key ==orders== items in a partition",
                "**Query**: one partition key, plus `begins_with`, `between`, ordering",
                "**Scan**: whole table, slow, costly, avoid in production"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "table.query(",
                "  KeyConditionExpression=Key('pk').eq('u1')",
                "  & Key('sk').begins_with('ORDER#'))"
              ],
              "note": "one partition, sort-key prefix"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. GSI vs LSI",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "GSI",
                "LSI"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Keys",
                  "New partition + sort",
                  "Same partition, new sort"
                ],
                [
                  "Created",
                  "==Anytime==",
                  "Table creation only"
                ],
                [
                  "Limits",
                  "20; own capacity; eventually consistent only",
                  "5; 10 GB per partition"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Non-key attribute?** Add a ==GSI== on it",
                "**Query vs Scan?** One partition key vs whole table",
                "**GSI vs LSI?** Anytime and 20 vs creation-only and 5",
                "**Hot partition?** High-cardinality, evenly accessed partition key"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Capacity Modes and Choosing RDS vs DynamoDB",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Capacity Modes and Choosing RDS vs DynamoDB",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Capacity Modes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "On-demand",
                "Provisioned"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Pay",
                  "per request",
                  "set RCU + WCU"
                ],
                [
                  "Planning",
                  "none, absorbs spikes",
                  "auto scaling available"
                ],
                [
                  "Best for",
                  "new or unpredictable traffic",
                  "steady, cheaper"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "1 ==RCU== = one strongly consistent 4 KB read/s (two eventually consistent)",
                "1 ==WCU== = one 1 KB write/s",
                "100 strong reads of 8 KB/s = 2 RCU each = ==200 RCU==",
                "Provisioned → on-demand: ==4 times== per rolling 24 h; back: any time",
                "Over limit: `ProvisionedThroughputExceededException`, retry with backoff"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. RDS or DynamoDB",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "RDS",
                "DynamoDB"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Queries",
                  "joins, ad-hoc SQL",
                  "known access patterns, key lookups"
                ],
                [
                  "Transactions",
                  "large, complex relational",
                  "ACID, up to 100 items / 4 MB"
                ],
                [
                  "Fit",
                  "existing engine compatibility",
                  "massive scale, predictable latency"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Design the DynamoDB table around its queries"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Relational schema",
              "text": "Modelling DynamoDB like relational tables forces ==Scans==. Design keys from the queries first."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
